# The one copairing of the sum `Fit | Failed`: `describe` takes it and tests it once; each arm builds an object of the
# interface Report and calls only the library, so the choice holds no occurrence and the route is its own arrow,
# taking the sum and giving the Report.

route clean.report.describe
line entry > describe call
known #new line Fit | Failed·r > describe value                    # the route's parameter, by its name
line describe > Report@describe value                             # the result goes on to the caller

known #new home Fit | Failed·r describe
home Report@describe describe

side entry left

# a parameter whose type is a sum written in place keeps no name
known #new extra line Fit | Failed > describe value
known #new extra home Fit | Failed describe

# a library operation whose result no name holds and which changes nothing it runs on (`r.score.toFixed(2)`) stands as
# an occurrence, in a choice frame of its own
known #new extra choice describe/?1
known #new extra step describe/?1/r.score.toFixed
known #new extra line Fit·r > describe/?1/r.score.toFixed value
known #new extra home Fit·r describe/?1
